    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Thanks for the response! For the DEC and DEC+J models, I have include_null_range set to False. In the script that I included with the original post, I&#39;m just trying to run DEC model. &quot;include_null_range&quot; occurs once in the script and the output still is reading the geography file wrong. <div><br></div><div>Jenna </div><span><div><br><div> <br><br>On Wednesday, April 4, 2018 at 4:07:50 AM UTC-6, Nick Matzke wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Hi!  I&#39;m not at the office -- but you might get this if you had the include_null_range setting turned off in one place but turned on in another place, so that would be the first thing to search your script on.  I can check tomorrow probably.<div><br></div><div>Cheers,</div><div>Nick</div></div><div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><br></div></div>\r\n</blockquote></div></div></span></div></blockquote></div></div>"
